The module `mohs-cron` (package io.mohs.cron) is adapted from
org.springframework.scheduling.support of the Spring Framework. The
adaptation moves the classes into io.mohs.cron, replaces the internal
org.springframework.util helpers with the reduced Assert/StringUtils in
the same package, and restores org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable. One
functional divergence from upstream is documented in
QuartzCronField#nextOrSame: the roll-forward is retried in a loop against
the seed, so that next() cannot return its own argument for "L-n"
day-of-month expressions. Every adapted file carries the original Apache
License header plus a note describing its changes.
